{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791366068,"nonce":"IixejNvOkyYdLWQC8x3JiCxijM0=","title":"Expression metadata consumes lower-precedence operators","message":"After the Dynamic array slot fix, TestOps reaches its final assertions and computes 5 * @foo 3 + 4 as 35 instead of 19; nested metadata has the same result. parser/src/rd/expr.rs parse_unary parses a whole expression after metadata, so the addition becomes part of the right-hand multiplication operand.\n\nNative Haxe macro AST probes in /tmp/rayzor-metadata-precedence/MetadataPrecedence.hx show metadata binds to a unary operand: @foo 3 + 4 is Add(Meta(3),4), -@foo 3 + 4 is Add(Neg(Meta(3)),4), and metadata on a ternary condition stays on the condition. Parentheses retain explicit grouping. Assignment is special: @foo x = 1 and @foo x += 1 wrap the entire assignment in metadata, preserving annotations such as @:move and @:await on assignment expressions. Probe logs: /tmp/rayzor-metadata-precedence/native-shapes-expanded.log.\n\nFix unary metadata precedence while retaining assignment wrapping, and verify arithmetic, nested metadata, parentheses, unary operators, ternary conditions, and macro-visible assignment annotations. TestOps should then pass once the erased array checkpoint lands.","files":null}]}